    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20763" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hir</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ir</span></b> ,
			indecl.
		n.
		from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χείρ</span>, like heres from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῆρος</span>, and hiems from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χεῖμα, χειμών</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a hand</i>: quibu'
			vinum Defusum e pleno siet, ir siphove, cui nil Dempsit, i. e. <i>the palm of the hand</i>, <i>used in
				tasting wine</i>, Lucil. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fin.
				2, 8, 23</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Charis. p. 12</span></i>
			P.; <i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 648</span></i> ib.; 698 ib.</div>
